quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  21,82,And among the devils (some were made subservient) who dove for him (into the seas) and accomplished tasks other than that. And We were watchful over them.
  21,83,"And (remember) Ayyub (Job) when he called his Lord: ‘Indeed suffering has befallen me, and You are the Most Merciful of the merciful.’"
  21,84,"So We responded to him and removed his suffering. And We gave him (back) his family, along with others like them, as a mercy from Us and a reminder for the worshippers."
  21,85,"And (remember) Isma‘il (Ishmael), Idris (Enoch) and Dhu al-Kifl; each of them was among the patient."
  21,86,"And We admitted them into Our mercy. Indeed, they were among the righteous."
  21,87,"And (remember) Dhu al-Nun*, when he went away angrily, thinking that We would not put him to hardship (on his journey). Then he called (Us) in the darkness: ‘There is no god except You. Glory be to You! I have indeed been among those who wrong (their souls).’"
  21,88,So We responded to him and delivered him from grief. And that is how We save the believers.
  21,89,"And (remember) Zakariyya (Zachariah) when he called to his Lord: ‘My Lord! Do not leave me alone (i.e. childless), though You are the best of inheritors.’"
  21,90,"So We responded to him and gave him Yahya (John), and We cured (the infertility of) his wife for him. Indeed, they were always quick in (performing) good deeds. And they would supplicate Us, in hope and in fear, and they were always humble before Us."
